From 29f95ec9732e49697f2b672bae89e91e7fe197b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 12:35:19 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gates): make validate/preflight fail-closed (B2/N1)

A gate that manufactures false confidence is worse than no gate. Three
false-green paths are closed:

1. validate runAllTests: a bun run that executes 0 tests reported
   "Tests: PASS". It now returns an explicit SKIP (never PASS) when 0
   tests are found, and says so when the runner is absent. runAllTests
   takes an injectable exec for testing.
2. preflight base resolution: a fresh repo with no origin/HEAD computed
   "0 changed files" and passed every gate vacuously. New strict
   resolveChangeSet distinguishes "resolved base, genuinely no changes"
   from "no base branch" and fails closed with a remedy on the latter.
3. preflight structural gate: it hard-ran Forge's OWN internal test
   paths (skills-sync-drift, _resolve-command-opts, sync-agentic-workflow)
   which a consumer repo can never satisfy. It now runs only the
   artifacts that exist in the target repo and reports an explicit SKIP
   in a consumer context. The runner honors a skipped gate outcome.

Kernel: 12b00157-07a2-4431-99c2-14dd640eb225

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
